 lumen. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6P9B6","text":"Activates an alternative mTOR signaling pathway through RPS6KB2 activation and EIF4EBP1 repression to regulate cell proliferation and migration (PubMed:29750193). Recruits MTOR at the lysosome, essential for MTOR signaling at the lysosome (PubMed:29750193). Binds to the vacuolar-type ATPase (V-ATPase) complex, triggering a conformational change and is likely to regulate its activity (PubMed:35672408, PubMed:35994636). No effect on V-ATPase activity was observed in vitro in one study although it was suggested that it may have inhibitory activity in vivo (PubMed:35672408). However, another study showed that it can promote V-ATPase activity (PubMed:38593795). Protects neuronal cells against oxidative stress (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}